<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Lindum Reefs gold mine falls into Q2 loss.</title>
<headline>Lindum Reefs gold mine falls into Q2 loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss before capital spending   0.49  vs 3.06 profit</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 0.30  vs 0.28</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			  467  vs 535</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled/treated	     298,000  vs 264,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			   1.57  vs 2.03</p>
<p>    Working costs			   22.81  vs 24.29</p>
<p>    Revenue from gold		     22.86  vs 27.53</p>
<p>Full name: Lindum Reefs Gold Mining Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that the lower gold price has impacted significantly on the current pay reserves position. Lindum Reefs will re-evaluate its options as regards the current mining plan, it said. All efforts will be made within the constraints of opencast mining to maximise grade and reduce mining costs, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
